redfin 1090: experiment E1 "AP loopback" over the AFE RT proxy ports (coder V, 2026-11-14). research/cc/BBA-design-study.md B1-B3.
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy 0 (default: today's direct path, nothing new runs) / 1: at the next call start the AFE RT proxy
  ports 0x2000 (RX, downlink read by the AP) / 0x2001 (TX, uplink written by the AP) come up (register RT driver,
  map 32 KB, RT_PROXY_CONFIG 16 kHz mono 16 bit 10 ms, start), the session starts as today, then the CVP is switched
  (MVM PAUSE, CVP SET_DEVICE_V3, media info, commit, START). The kernel loops the PCM: downlink -> sweet_sound.c's
  playback stream in "call mode" (3 x 10 ms periods instead of 8 x 20 ms) -> 0x9040 + the call's amplifier; mic ring
  (0x9001, 48 kHz) averaged to 16 kHz -> 0x2001. Any failure falls back to 0x9001/0x9040 in the same start.
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy_opts: 1 CVP created on the proxy ports (no switch), 2 8 kHz, 4 host-PCM probe (status only).
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy_stats (RO): frames/s, gaps, ring fills, under/overruns, slips; DTMF latency line.
- sweet_adsp.c: redwood_adsp_apr_events_proxy() (AFE handler asked first; NULL unless a proxy call runs).
- New file bsd/dev/sweet_vproxy.c (the AP side), sweet_mic.c redwood_mic_voice_peek(), sweet_sound.c call mode.

